# NocoDB Enterprise Features Development Roadmap and Task List

This document outlines a comprehensive roadmap and granular task list for developing enterprise features for the NocoDB project from scratch, leveraging Claude Code (Minimax m2.7). The development process will adopt a modular and plugin-based approach, aiming for minimal interference with the existing NocoDB open-source codebase.

## 1. General Approach and Tools

This section details the overarching strategy, development environment, and tools to be utilized throughout the project.

-   **Development Environment:** Development will occur within the NocoDB monorepo structure, specifically under a new directory such as `packages/nc-enterprise` or a similar designation, to maintain separation from the core open-source components.
-   **Code Generation:** The Claude Code (Minimax m2.7) model will be extensively used to generate code snippets, test cases, API definitions, and documentation drafts for each task. The model's large context window will be instrumental in understanding NocoDB's existing codebase and producing compatible, high-quality code.
-   **Technology Stack:** The project will adhere to the existing NocoDB technology stack, which includes NestJS/TypeScript for the backend, Nuxt.js/Vue.js for the frontend, and Knex.js for the ORM, ensuring consistency and leveraging established patterns.
-   **Testing Strategy:** Comprehensive testing will be integrated into the development lifecycle. This includes writing unit and integration tests for every generated code piece, and planning for End-to-End (E2E) tests using Playwright to ensure functional correctness and system stability.
-   **Documentation:** For each feature, a technical design document, API documentation, and user guide drafts will be created. This ensures clarity, maintainability, and ease of use for both developers and end-users.

